<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-cooke-clock-and-wavefront-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cooke & Zeeman (1976) clock-and-wavefront somite segmentation — MorphoEval overall 90.1/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 post-remediation evaluation of `1976-cooke-clock-and-wavefront.py` (90.4/100, up from 58.4/100 in Pass 1; +32.0 overall). The remediated script integrates the Thom-Zeeman cusp catastrophe wavefront ODE tau_chi*dchi/dt = -(chi^3 - a(x,t)*chi - b_osc(x,t)) with proportional wavefront transition scaling, achieving 0.13% somite wavelength accuracy (S_sim = 100.13 um vs S = 100.0 um, CV = 0.0025), exact somite count invariance across normal (L = 4.0 mm, N = 40) and miniature (L = 2.4 mm, S = 60.08 um, N = 40) embryos, a clock-doubled perturbation (T_c = 90 min -> N = 20, S = 200.25 um), a clock-arrested negative control (A_clock = 0 -> 0 somites), and automated bilateral DoG somite segmentation on `somite_embryo_specimen.jpg` (8 upper and 9 lower somites, mean spacing 48.47 px, bilateral symmetry ratio 0.9605), backed by 3 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems in `Loop_021_clock_and_wavefront.lean`. Overall 90.1/100 (faithfulness 89.6, reproducibility 91.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 317bc3c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 93, Morphological realism / specimen match 87, Parameter expressivity 89, Morphometric validation 90, Source and data traceability 93, Code-to-model traceability 91, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/clock_and_wavefront_comparison.png: rendered output of 1976-cooke-clock-and-wavefront.py at 317bc3c, image/png, 1215618 B, 2310×1372 px, artifact_sha256 1db23a76c4cc9d4544515fc51d9b8e774a6986c84596f4234ab2cf361bf10101 (sha256 1db23a76c4cc9d4544515fc51d9b8e774a6986c84596f4234ab2cf361bf10101), spec_fingerprint 9a567843f2a6020e93562e6d7e58c2b8167adcb8c6b198fb2164e03a085e6bb6. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 9a567843f2a6020e93562e6d7e58c2b8167adcb8c6b198fb2164e03a085e6bb6; artifact_sha256: 1db23a76c4cc9d4544515fc51d9b8e774a6986c84596f4234ab2cf361bf10101; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/clock_and_wavefront/clock_and_wavefront_reference.json=4851550f4179ae63..., datasets/clock_and_wavefront/scout_manifest.json=0beabd3277c705e6..., datasets/clock_and_wavefront/somite_embryo_specimen.jpg=8b80971796cb29e2...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-clock-and-wavefront-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Cooke & Zeeman (1976) J. Theor. Biol. 58:455-476 kinematic somite wavelength law S = v * T_c and Thom-Zeeman cusp catastrophe wavefront manifold | Cooke (1975) Nature 254:196-199 Xenopus laevis blastula size-reduction invariance (N ~ 40 somites across normal and miniature embryos); reconstructed_in_script: 1D anteroposterior Thom-Zeeman cusp catastrophe ODE tau_chi*dchi/dt = -(chi^3 - a(x,t)*chi - b_osc(x,t)) with proportional wavefront width scaling | Bilateral dorsal somite row DoG peak and inter-somitic cleft segmentation on somite_embryo_specimen.jpg (48.47 px mean spacing, symmetry ratio 0.9605); transfer_boundary: 1D anteroposterior paraxial mesoderm axis mapped to dorsal vertebrate SEM somite rows; does_not_claim: Full 3D viscoelastic epithelialization mechanics of somite rosette boundary rotation or explicit Delta-Notch intercellular delay coupling (covered in Slots 022-023)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Couple the 1D Thom-Zeeman cusp wavefront to a 2D vertex-model paraxial mesoderm sheet to simulate epithelial rosette cleft rotation.",
        "remediation needed: Integrate spatial FGF8/Wnt3a vs Retinoic Acid reaction-diffusion bistability (Goldbeter et al. 2007) to derive wavefront velocity v endogenously from posterior tailbud elongation." ;
    pk:hasScore 9.01e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-cooke-clock-and-wavefront-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cooke & Zeeman (1976) clock-and-wavefront somite segmentation — Parameter expressivity: 89/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Evaluates 5 experimental regimes from Cooke (1975) and Cooke & Zeeman (1976) (normal 4.0 mm, reduced 3.0 mm, miniature 2.4 mm, 2x clock period T_c=90 min, and 1.5x wavefront velocity), maps the continuous 2D parameter morphospace S(v, T_c) = v * T_c across v in [1.0, 3.6] um/min and T_c in [25, 100] min (Panel C), compares proportional wavefront scaling (v ~ L) against an unscaled wavefront failure control (v = v_0, Panel D), and includes a clock-arrested ablation control (A_clock = 0 -> 0 somites, Panel B) plus CLI flags (`--L-mm`, `--Tc-min`, `--T-total-min`, `--seed`)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
